invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_mont.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh x86-kernels
reason: rsa_vp1_cpu asks for AVX2 before AVX-512 IFMA, so a session whose
  ch_cfg.cpu holds both bits runs the AVX2 kernel, which took more time
  than the IFMA kernel on every runner that had both. The bytes are the
  same, so no vector sees it. bin/x86_kernels_test counts the calls into
  each kernel under each value, on stand-ins that run no kernel
  instruction, and requires the IFMA kernel's call where the value holds
  its bit. Only an x86-64 object holds the two dispatches, so the lane
  builds the binary for x86-64; it skips without docker, and this then
  reports unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
    if (use_ifma(cpu) && kernel_takes(n, n_len, RSA_IFMA_WORDS_MIN)) {
--- new
    if (use_ifma(cpu) && !use_avx2(cpu) && kernel_takes(n, n_len, RSA_IFMA_WORDS_MIN)) {
